# Gate step 1968-psy9 — the git mirror sends READY right after its seed
# fetch; the per-ref startup retry-push runs after it, in the background, and
# is skipped with one line when there is no upstream credential. Measured on
# yoga 2026-11-02: READY waited 49.3 s for 1489 refused pushes on every warm
# launch. The arms execute the real functions cut out of
# images/git/entrypoint.sh over a scratch mirror; no podman, no network.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the git mirror sends READY before its startup retry-push (1968-psy9)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/test-git-mirror-ready-before-retry-push.lua"
STEP_ERROR="the git mirror again holds READY behind the startup retry-push, or pushes every ref without an upstream credential (1968-psy9) — see the FAIL lines above"
STEP_OK="git mirror READY-before-retry-push fixture passed"
